Done. Here's what was implemented:

**`teamai/src/app/actions/mcp.ts`** — new server actions module:
- Exports `McpServerEntry` interface (`command`, optional `args`, `env`, and `type: 'stdio'`)
- Exports `McpConfig` interface (`mcpServers: Record<string, McpServerEntry>`)
- Module-level `DEFAULT = { mcpServers: {} }`
- `getMcpConfig()`: reads `<projectRoot>/.mcp.json` via `getActiveProjectPath()`, returns `DEFAULT` on any error (ENOENT, SyntaxError, etc.)
- `saveMcpConfig(config)`: writes pretty-printed JSON to `<projectRoot>/.mcp.json`, then calls `revalidatePath('/settings')`

**`teamai/tests/unit/mcp-actions.test.ts`** — 7 passing tests covering:
- `getMcpConfig` returns DEFAULT when file is absent
- `getMcpConfig` returns DEFAULT when file contains invalid JSON (AC-12)
- `getMcpConfig` returns parsed config for valid JSON (including env vars)
- `saveMcpConfig` writes pretty-printed JSON to the correct path
- `saveMcpConfig` calls `revalidatePath('/settings')` after writing
- `saveMcpConfig` overwrites existing config
